### Role 3: Super Admin / System Administrator

The **Super Admin** role holds master administrative control over multi-tenant database settings, global statutory wage ceilings, system seeder parameters, and user role permissions.

| Feature / Module | Scope & Functionality | What the Super Admin Can Do |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Global Permission Bypass** | System-wide RBAC | Inherits all permissions across all companies without restriction (`HasPermission` evaluates to `true`). |
| **Statutory Ceiling Configuration** | `appsettings.json` & DI `PayrollSettings` | Modify system-wide EPF wage ceiling (default ₹15,000), ESIC wage ceiling (default ₹21,000), Bonus ceiling (₹21,000), and Gratuity max limit (₹20,000,000). |
| **Database Migration & Auto-Seeding** | [Program.cs](file:///d:/hhrrmmsss/IndiaHRMS/backend/src/IndiaHRMS.API/Program.cs#L22-L38) & [DatabaseSeeder.cs](file:///d:/hhrrmmsss/IndiaHRMS/backend/src/IndiaHRMS.API/DatabaseSeeder.cs) | Run EF Core migrations, auto-create master databases (`IndiaHRMS_Clean`), and seed initial Super Admin credentials (`admin` / `Admin@123`). |
| **Hangfire Background Job Console** | `/hangfire` Dashboard | Monitor background job queues for monthly EL leave accruals, auto-marking absent records, and automated notifications. |

